Hi, you can obtain this (most easily) using the compare_solutions_mplus() function. Here is an example that will return a data frame with the VLMR statistic and p-value (the key is to add return_stats_df = TRUE as an argument to the function):

compare_solutions_mplus(iris, Sepal.Length, Sepal.Width, Petal.Length, Petal.Width,
                        n_profiles_max = 4, return_stats_df = TRUE)

Note that in the data frame, the statistic and p-value are labeled as VLMR, but in an older version of the documentation, there is an argument for LMR; this provides both VLMR and LMR output (via TECH11 LMR), but the VLMR output is what is used, so I just changed the name of the argument to VLMR to be more clear.

Also, if you have an older version, be sure to update using install.packages("tidyLPA") or devtools::install_github("jrosen48/tidyLPA") (for the most recent, development version).

Please let me know if this works for you!
Josh

