Dear Josh and others,

My preference would be to drop the dependency on colorbrewer, and use ggplot’s standard color palette. Users can always override the color palette later, after our package returns a healthy ggplot object. No need to enforce a specific package and introduce an additional dependency on colorbrewer if it’s going to throw errors.

What do you guys think?

Best,

Caspar

