Hi all, sorry for the slow involvement in this earlier convo. - one thing I'm having trouble understanding is where RColorBrewer entered the picture. I don't think we (deliberately) used or relied on the package; is ggplot2 using this as a default?

Muhammad, thanks so much for your message. I am guessing that the reason Ran's code gave that warning is that he wrote it to be used in the package (and in a function), so it's misbehaving when being run interactively.

Hopefully we can troubleshoot this soon. I'm submitting my dissertation in the next few weeks so will definitely have more time after :) In the meantime, one possible solution (albeit, one that is a bit more work), is to simply use the output of the estimate_profiles() function, and then to write your own function to plot the profiles. Like I said, a bit more work! I'm also curious whether you can simply modify the result of plot_profiles() - I think this outputs a ggplot object, so can you add a different scale? Sorry if this is akin to what Ran suggested.

Have a good weekend, hoping to get this fixed.
josh

