Thanks Caspar (and Ran and Muhammad).I just removed this line. You can install the development version with:

install.packages("devtools")
devtools::install_github("jrosen48/tidyLPA")

As Ran found, if you add:

scale_fill_brewer("", type = "qual", palette = "Set3")

To the object returned by plot_profiles(), then you can use the (old) color palette for up to 12 variables. I.e.,

estimate_profiles(iris,
    Sepal.Length, Sepal.Width, Petal.Length, Petal.Width,
    model = 1,
    n_profiles = 3) %>%
    plot_profiles() +

    scale_fill_brewer("", type = "qual", palette = "Set3")

But as Capar says, without that added line, the plots should have the default ggplot colors.

Muhammad (and Ran, if you like), can you install the development version (with the two lines of code above) and say if this works?

Thank you,
Josh

